/.idea
**/.DS_STORE

# Per-account Claude dirs hold plugin caches and session state.
# Ignore their contents explicitly, then allow only the files that are symlinked back
# into ~/.claude-<account>/ so repo edits reach the account directly.
# Each account CLAUDE.md is a thin profile that imports the shared rules from
# home/.config/claude-shared/core.md (linked to ~/.config/claude-shared by the XDG loop).
# settings.json is tracked AND written by Claude Code at runtime. It must stay secret-free:
# its `env` block does NOT expand $VAR and it OVERRIDES shell exports, so a credential there
# would be both literal and wrong. Secrets live in ~/.config/claude/{common,<account>}.env,
# outside the repo. Claude Code reads no user-level settings.local.json, and autoMode is read
# only from settings.json, so autoMode entries stay generic: no customer, repo or host names.
/home/.claude-*/*
!/home/.claude-*/CLAUDE.md
!/home/.claude-*/settings.json
